[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-1.5,0)--(5.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.5)--(0,5.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (5);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,4);
\coordinate (A) at (5,0);
\draw[thick,blue] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left]{$r=5$};
\fill[red] (P) circle (2.5pt) node[above right]{$P(3,4)$};
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=1cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle = A--O--P};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
The point $P(3,4)$ lies on a circle of radius $r=5$ centred at the origin. Write down the exact values of $\cos\theta$, $\sin\theta$, and $\tan\theta$.

